Z||000000||pureSKID||11-07-2001||07:05 PM||||What are the engine options available to swap into a Fiero, while using the stock transmission, stock wiring, or carburated set up.<P>I don't know much about many v8s... so list the hp/tq figures along with which cars that engine came in.<P>I read lots about the 4.9 caddy and 305 chev engines being put in but they are kinda low on HP.  I'm expecting 200+ hp without mods.<P>The Buick GN v6 turbo engine looks good...how about it? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||fastback87||11-08-2001||12:27 PM||||you ought to be able to get 200hp out of your stock engine...If I were looking for a V8 I would expect closer to 500HP!!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||KRMFiero||11-08-2001||02:28 PM||||Let see.... 3.1, 3.4 (OHV), 4.1, 4.5, 4.9 (the 4.x's require minum wiring), 3800 i guess... carbed 3.8s are suppost to be direct bolt in.....   basically any BOP bolt pattern engine will bolt to the Fieros Tranny and there is plenty of room in the compartment so you pretty much only have to worry about Wiring, Motor mounts (easy to make for Fiero) and if it is RWD or FWD (Starters are on opposite sides so you will have to drill new holes if engine is from a RWD)<P><BR>Kyle||||reg||1
